      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just a heads up, there is a slight difference in how the state name vs state ID functions work:\n\n`pdc_power_mgmt_get_task_state_name()` has a special case where the transitional CMD_START and CMD_WAIT states get translated into the return states, so that the caller only ever sees the actual permanent states (unattached, attached source, attached sink, suspended, type-c only, etc). The use case is the `pdc status` console command where we only care about what the port is doing.\n\n`pdc_power_mgmt_get_task_state()` returns the raw state. This might cause the tests to encounter the ephemeral states like CMD_WAIT and could lead to flakiness if the tests are not expecting that or aren\u0027t polling. It\u0027s probably okay since they are using `wait_state_name`, though.",
      "revId": "f4a09ea00efeb1f1fd65def89f8ac624e4715f6a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
